= Agent memory (artificial intelligence) — Technical =

== Memory loop ==
An agent-memory subsystem can be modeled as:

<pre>
observation / event
→ write decision
→ storage/update
→ indexing/organization
→ retrieval decision
→ read/recall
→ policy/action
</pre>

The write and read policies can be learned or rule-based.

== Dimensions ==
Current literature classifies memory along overlapping dimensions such as:

* temporal scope;
* factual versus experiential function;
* working-state versus persistent memory;
* token/external/parametric/latent representation;
* passive versus actively managed memory;
* individual versus shared multi-agent memory.

No single taxonomy is canonical.

== Failure modes ==
Memory systems can suffer from:

* stale facts;
* retrieval omission;
* irrelevant recall;
* contradictory records;
* privacy leakage;
* unbounded growth;
* self-reinforcing false summaries;
* incorrect consolidation or forgetting.

